{
  "id": "geo-transform",
  "chapterNumber": "9",
  "title": {
    "en": "Transformations &amp; Symmetry",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Rigid motions — translations, reflections and rotations — preserve size and shape; dilations scale a figure.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Transformations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Translations, reflections and rotations are rigid motions that preserve distance. A dilation by factor \\( k \\) scales lengths by \\( k \\) and areas by \\( k^{2} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Translation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "slide",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Reflection",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "flip",
              "ar": null
            },
            "wide": true
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Rotation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "turn",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Dilation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "scale by \\( k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Dilation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "geoDilateCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A triangle and its dilated image, scaled from the origin by a slider-controlled factor k",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "geoDilateDataBtn",
          "panelId": "geoDilateDataPanel",
          "descId": "geoDilateDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "geoDilateDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The scale factor and the resulting side length and area",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            { "en": "quantity", "ar": null },
            { "en": "value", "ar": null }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "geoDilateK",
            "label": { "en": "scale factor <b>k</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 0.25, "max": 3.5, "value": 3, "step": 0.25,
            "valueDisplayId": "geoDilateKval",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Dilation scale factor k", "ar": null }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "geoDilateLen",
            "label": { "en": "image side length", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "12.00"
          },
          {
            "id": "geoDilateArea",
            "label": { "en": "image area", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "54.000"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "The faint triangle has a side of length 4, dilated from the origin. Default k = 3 matches Worked example 9.A exactly (4 → 12). Length scales by k, but area scales by k² — drag k and watch the area readout grow much faster than the length one.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A dilation with scale factor \\( 3 \\) maps a side of length \\( 4 \\). Find the image length.</p>\\[ 3\\times 4=12. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
